//
// A "kitchen sink" example: a complete all-grain recipe that uses every top-level section of the format, and a brew
// log that fills in EVERY BrewLog field.  Because the schema forbids unevaluated properties, renaming or removing any
// field that this file uses will make it fail validation -- which is the point.
//
// Also exercises:
//  • Addition schedules at every stage (mash, boil, whirlpool, dry hop, package), using `step`, `time` and `duration`
//  • A water agent (gypsum) in the mash, and a fining agent in the boil
//  • Base and target water profiles, with a proportion of RO water
//  • Hop oil content, culture killer properties, and equipment with every vessel type except a separate lauter tun
//    (because the mash tun is also used for lautering), plus default batch size and foundation volume
//
